        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">For most people, start with the Ice Barrel 300</strong> and ice: it is
            rigid, insulated, made in the USA and ready for a chiller if you stick with it. Taller users should
            choose the Ice Barrel 500, buyers who want a chilled and heated tub in one piece the SaunaLife S1,
            and anyone unsure whether they will keep plunging The Cold Pod at about $150. Treat budget
            tub-and-chiller kits like the Recoverex as listing-only purchases and check the GFCI and warranty
            details first.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whatever you buy, check the floor, the outlet and your health before the tub, never plunge alone,
